    "Numerical reproducers used the existing boost_probe_classified executable and in-memory 100-digit Decimal calculations. No writes, spawning or heavy science.",
    "Unrelated dirty payloads, screen implementation, quadrature, solver integration and scientific admission excluded."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "location": "rust/rec_microphysics/src/frame.rs:72-76",
      "invariant": "Accepted velocities must produce accurate Lorentz factors and invariant-preserving boosts, or return NumericalDomainUncertain.",
      "evidence": "Reproducer: MaterialVelocity::new([0.6, 0.7999999999999998, 0.0]).unwrap().normal_to_material_four_vector([1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]). The rounded hypot norm yields gamma=67108864, whereas Decimal evaluation from the exact binary64 beta components gives 56717341.93959738. The returned vector has Minkowski norm approximately -1.4 instead of -1; inverse boosting returns [1.5, 0.29999999701976776, 0.3999999985098839, 0.0], all through Ok. Error under the supplied oracle's gross scaling is 4.0379e-10, exceeding 4096eps=9.0949e-13. Compute the residual defining gamma accurately or refuse this numerically uncertain domain.",
      "severity": "P2"
    },
    {
      "location": "rust/rec_microphysics/src/frame.rs:29-40",
      "invariant": "Destructive underflow must not silently return finite values outside the numerical tolerance.",
      "evidence": "The product and quotient guards detect only results rounded to zero. Reproducer: beta=[0.6,0,0], input=[f64::from_bits(3),0,0,0]. The existing probe returns forward components [f64::from_bits(4),-f64::from_bits(2),0,0]; inverse boosting returns time component f64::from_bits(4), rather than the original bits(3). Both calls return Ok. The supplied gross-scaled comparison gives error 0.0266667 versus tolerance 9.0949e-13. Detect destructive precision loss in nonzero subnormal arithmetic and return NumericalDomainUncertain, while retaining accurately representable subnormal cases.",
      "severity": "P2"
    },
    {
      "location": "rust/rec_microphysics/src/frame.rs:233-239",
      "invariant": "The force adapter must return the distinct NormalFourForce promised by FRAME_BRIDGE.md:9.",
      "evidence": "The method instead returns and constructs MaterialFourForce; NormalFourForce is unused. A caller declaring `let normal: NormalFourForce = v.material_four_force_to_normal(force).unwrap();` fails type checking. Conversely, the returned normal-frame components remain accepted as material-frame input for another boost. Change the return type and constructed value to NormalFourForce, and explicitly bind that type in the existing force test.",
      "severity": "P2"
    }
  ]
}
